// The capybara game (a working title; design.md is its brief): the first level, and the movement
// lab beside it. The sim ticks 120 times a second on the ticker's thread (`engine::run`), and each
// frame draws the snapshots round its time in flat 2D, seen straight on (art.wrela has the
// passes): the sky and the zoo behind (scenery.wrela), the ground and its grass (earth.wrela),
// the zoo's signs, which teach the moves where they're first needed (signs.wrela), the cast and
// its particles (cast.wrela, sprites.wrela, dust.wrela), the water (waves.wrela), and over it all
// the screens (screens.wrela). The music (music.wrela) and the game's sounds (sound.wrela) start
// on the first frame.
//
// The game opens on the level's title; Esc, P or a controller's Start pauses on a menu: resume,
// restart, the runs, the options and the controls. The pages and their focus are the sim's
// (world.wrela); the frames draw them, with the keys or the controller's buttons the player last
// used (ui::glyphs), and publish each as a semantic tree, so a click or a screen reader works
// them too. While playing, the screen holds only the snacks' count at the top left, and the clock
// at the top right if the options show it (off at first). The options (the music, the clock, the
// ghost) and the moves the signs have seen made are the player's settings, kept in the game's
// storage (settings.wrela). F3 shows the frame rate and the render scale; M turns the music off
// and on, the sounds playing on. Keys: the arrows or W A S D to move (down slides or crouches; in
// water up and down swim, and in turn dolphin kick), Space, Z or K to jump (again in the air for
// the double jump; in water, a kick), R to restart, Tab for the other course (the level or the
// lab). A controller: the stick or pad, South or East to jump, Select to restart.
//
// Runs (replay.wrela): each finished attempt is a replay, and the best few of each category are
// kept in the game's storage. The menu's Runs shows them: two boards, the player's runs and the
// tool-assisted runs (the route search's, made by a program, never ranked with a player's), each
// any% and 100%. Choosing a run watches it (watch.wrela). The ghost that runs beside the player
// (the options) is their best, a tool-assisted run, or none; with the clock shown, each
// checkpoint's split is against it.
//
// For an agent: `wrela-host <build> --frames n --input script.json --png out.png` draws frame n
// on the GPU (scripts.wrela has scripts), and `capybara` exports the capybara's state for `wrela
// trace --watch capybara`, which needs a toolchain whose trace runs the ticker in lockstep.

